  "pending_scope": {
    "R1-13": {
      "variant": "A",
      "exact_text": "Representative datasets relevant to expressive label recovery. “MIDI / note annotations” includes performance MIDI and aligned note annotations convertible to MIDI; it does not by itself imply measured velocity. “Velocity” indicates the availability of the note-level dynamics target, with qualifications stated in the row notes. “Score” refers to a reference symbolic score, rather than the performance timing in MIDI. A triangle marks a qualification in the corresponding row."
    },
    "R1-21": {
      "variant": "A",
      "exact_text": "Performance MIDI supplies captured velocity targets for training, while the completion interface can also accept quantised symbolic input. The composition use case is to add a velocity profile while retaining the notes and timing supplied by the user."
    },
    "R1-26": {
      "variant": "A",
      "exact_text": "In Table 4.1, audio denotes the standalone HPT velocity branch. The score-informed rows add either the frame-wise BiLSTM or the onset-token Transformer correction module. The onset condition uses the score onset matrix O; onset + frame additionally supplies the active-note matrix F; and onset + frame_ex uses F − O to distinguish sustain from the onset frame."
    },
    "R1-30": {
      "variant": "B",
      "exact_text": "Piece-disjoint cross-validation tests generalisation to unseen mazurkas within MazurkaBL. Cross-dataset evaluation additionally tests the learned mapping under changes in repertoire, performers, recording conditions, and annotation conventions. These factors vary together in Vienna4x22 and Batik-plays-Mozart, so the experiment diagnoses combined corpus transfer rather than isolating a composer or performer effect."
    }
  },
